+  {
+   "cell_type": "markdown",
+   "id": "687a62a7",
+   "metadata": {},
+   "source": [
+    "# Gradients\n",
+    "\n",
+    "`Gradients` helps differentiate through GTSAM, for example to learn factor\n",
+    "parameters from a loss evaluated on optimized estimates. The application\n",
+    "provides loss derivatives on the estimates, and parameterized factors provide\n",
+    "derivatives of their raw factor residuals. `Gradients` combines these to return\n",
+    "a loss gradient for a requested parameter vector, including the noise weighting.\n",
+    "\n",
+    "Two noisy observations provide a worked example of learning an observation\n",
+    "parameter. The [Python tutorial](../../../python/gtsam/examples/nonlinear/GradientsExample.ipynb)\n",
+    "extends the workflow to odometry calibration and a training update. The\n",
+    "mathematical derivation is in the final advanced section.\n",
+    "\n",
+    "The [PyTorch tutorial](../../../python/gtsam/examples/nonlinear/GradientsPyTorchExample.ipynb)\n",
+    "trains a small MLP through several factor graphs using raw factor VJPs."
+   ]
+  },
+  {
+   "cell_type": "markdown",
+   "id": "gradients-guide-copyright",
+   "metadata": {
+    "tags": [
+     "remove-cell"
+    ]
+   },
+   "source": [
+    "GTSAM Copyright 2010-2026, Georgia Tech Research Corporation,\n",
+    "Atlanta, Georgia 30332-0415\n",
+    "All Rights Reserved\n",
+    "\n",
+    "Authors: Frank Dellaert, et al. (see THANKS for the full author list)\n",
+    "\n",
+    "See LICENSE for the license information"
+   ]
+  },
+  {
+   "cell_type": "markdown",
+   "id": "gradients-guide-colab",
+   "metadata": {},
+   "source": [
+    "<a href=\"https://colab.research.google.com/github/borglab/gtsam/blob/develop/gtsam/nonlinear/doc/Gradients.ipynb\" target=\"_parent\"><img src=\"https://colab.research.google.com/assets/colab-badge.svg\" alt=\"Open In Colab\"/></a>"
+   ]
+  },
+  {
+   "cell_type": "code",
+   "execution_count": 1,
+   "id": "gradients-guide-install",
+   "metadata": {
+    "tags": [
