+{
+ "cells": [
+  {
+   "cell_type": "markdown",
+   "id": "693582c1",
+   "metadata": {},
+   "source": [
+    "# KnownLandmarkSquaredRangeFactor\n",
+    "\n",
+    "`KnownLandmarkSquaredRangeFactor` models a range measurement between an $N$-dimensional Euclidean point $x$ and a fixed known landmark $L$. Unlike `KnownLandmarkFactor`, it operates directly on a Euclidean point state and does not involve pose or orientation.\n",
+    "\n",
+    "A conventional range residual is\n",
+    "\n",
+    "$$\n",
+    "e_{\\text{range}}(x) = \\|x - L\\| - d,\n",
+    "$$\n",
+    "\n",
+    "where $d$ is the measured range. Note the residual is not polynomial in the state because the Euclidean norm contains a square root. Instead, `KnownLandmarkSquaredRangeFactor` uses the squared-range residual\n",
+    "\n",
+    "$$\n",
+    "e_{\\text{squared}}(x) = \\|x - L\\|^2 - d^2,\n",
+    "$$\n",
+    "\n",
+    "which is quadratic in $x$.\n",
+    "\n",
+    "The squared-range form is suitable for lifted QCQP formulations and subsequent semidefinite relaxations. If the semidefinite relaxation is tight, meaning that the lifted solution has the required rank, the relaxed problem recovers a globally optimal solution to the original QCQP.\n",
+    "\n",
+    "This factor currently provides the squared-range residual for standard GTSAM nonlinear optimization. QCQP/certifiable conversion is not yet implemented for this factor.\n",
+    "\n",
+    "For additional information on GTSAM's QCQP-to-SDP and chordal-sparsity framework, refer to *Exploiting Chordal Sparsity for Globally Optimal Estimation with Factor Graphs*.\n"
+   ]
+  },
+  {
+   "cell_type": "markdown",
+   "id": "fa13d829",
+   "metadata": {
+    "tags": [
+     "remove-cell"
+    ]
+   },
+   "source": [
+    "GTSAM Copyright 2010-2026, Georgia Tech Research Corporation, Atlanta, Georgia 30332-0415\n",
+    "All Rights Reserved\n",
+    "Authors: Frank Dellaert, et al. (see THANKS for the full author list)\n",
+    "See LICENSE for the license information"
+   ]
+  },
+  {
+   "cell_type": "markdown",
+   "id": "f871beec",
+   "metadata": {},
+   "source": [
+    "[![Open In Colab](https://colab.research.google.com/assets/colab-badge.svg)](https://colab.research.google.com/github/borglab/gtsam/blob/develop/gtsam/slam/doc/KnownLandmarkSquaredRangeFactor.ipynb)"
